"P1851003622" "Good job on buggin' them desks, suga'. Now we just gotta play the old waitin' game to see which one of our boys is the real traitor..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page MoralChoice Text :
"P801496866" "<color orange>Officer Pell coughs, trying to regain his composure.</color><br><br>H-hold on... just... hold on... ! I'll... tell you whatever you want to know..."
// Answer Text :
"P1162062197" "What are you doing working for the Syndicate?"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P1254580070" "Hah... the Syndicate... Cole thought he could wipe crime away. But now, they're stronger than ever. Smarter... better... they're better than us!<br><br>They work in the shadows, but soon, soon they'll bring Cole down. They're everywhere, {HeroName}!<br><br>They're not taking over through sheer brute force, like the Resistance, they're taking over from the inside!<br><br>Can't you see? Soon they'll all be controlling Cole, he'll have no choice but to follow them!"
// Answer Text :
"P536133512" "Not if I have anything to say about it."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P782357581" "It's too late to stop them now, {HeroName}. They're working together with the Resistance... they're going to move forward with the biggest plot to date.<br><br>The explosives here... they're going to put on a <i>big</i> show in Nova. In <color yellow>Cole Memorial Hospital</color>. Ask yourself, {HeroName}... how will the people look at Cole... if they see their beloved hospital go up in flames?<br><br>He won't be their protector anymore, their savior... they'll see Cole for who he really is... that he's just a man! No matter how powerful he becomes, he is still just a man!<br><br>And all men, {HeroName}, must eventually be brought down."
// Answer Text :
"P1775651159" "You're out of your mind! Blowing up a hospital to prove a point?"
// Page BlowupHospital Text :
"P4185494520" "Don't you try to say... that I'm some sort of psychopath, that I'm a monster!<br><br>Do you know how many people Cole has killed on a weekly basis, just to protect his utopia?! Lives of innocents will be lost, that much is true... but we will free the people of this city from the grip of Cole! We will give them what they long for - freedom!<br><br>If this were a true war, a war that was fought in the open, those people in the hospital would GLADLY give their lives to see our ideals come to life! But since we fight from the shadows, we must make that choice for them.<br><br>It's not too late for you though, {HeroName}. You can still help us, you can still join us!"
// Answer Text :
"P1235569606" "I'm here to protect the people of Praetoria, Pell. Unlike you."
// Page ProtectthePeople Text :
"P4219648710" "The people?! Bah!<br><br>The people have become mindless sheep to a super-powered shepherd! The people you're looking to protect are nothing but toys that Cole uses for his own amusement!<br><br>You think I'm a monster, but you, you {HeroName}, you're the real monster for siding with Cole!<br><br>So just go ahead, finish me off. I know how the system works.<br><br>I won't be left alive for treason against the state, so just finish me off here and now."
// Answer Text :
"P168382345" "It's not my place to sentence you. Your fellow officers will be here to do that."
// Answer Text :
"P4173795529" "You made the decision to do this, Pell. You leave me no choice! (Kill Pell)"
// Page MercyShown Text :
"P2078846135" "You're just delaying my fate, {HeroName}! You had better pray that I don't escape... if I do... I'll find you. I swear I'll find you and stop at least one more of Cole's dogs!"
// Answer Text :
"P669480065" "I'll be waiting, Pell."
// Page KillPell Text :
"P2381119451" "<color orange>Using your powers to swiftly carry out Pell's sentence for attacking the people of Praetoria.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P858966999" "Goodbye, Pell."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Cleopatra 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P4081816203" "Hey there suga', what happened? I sent some boys of mine to the ball, but they said Pell wasn't there."
// Answer Text :
"P760553803" "Pell's dead. And the Syndicate are working with the Resistance."
// Answer Text :
"P175466546" "Pell's with the PPD now. He was working with the Syndicate, not Resistance."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P1439758104" "<color orange>You explain to Cleopatra the events that happened within the warehouse.</color><br><br>I... see. Well, suga', you did right, takin' him down on the spot. S'what you gotta do against traitors, he knew what he was getting into when he decided that blowing up a <i>hospital</i> was a good idea. You and me, suga', we got ourselves a job to do. Savin' those people in the hospital."
// Answer Text :
"P2840620893" "Let's get to work."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P1116247330" "<color orange>You explain to Cleopatra the events that happened within the warehouse.</color><br><br>You're a better person than me, suga', I woulda ripped Pell's head off then and there. But I guess that's what makes us different. Regardless, we got ourselves a little job to do - savin' that hospital."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2670955662" "Hey suga', it looks like we got ourselves a catch from that bait we set out.<br><br>Looks like our boy is Officer Pell. He's been slippin' info to some guy named <color yellow>Grossman</color>. Now I ain't heard of a Crusader named Grossman, so I think this is another one of the Resistance's undercover agents. Accordin' to the computer, the little backstabber is organizin' a raid on a supply warehouse belongin' to Troy Altman. That's bad news for us, 'cause that warehouse contains explosives that Altman was plannin' on usin' to tear down some old buildings in Neutropolis!"
// AcceptString :
"P3550712653" "I'll get there before they can get away."
// SendOffString :
"P2632574359" "S'why I'm feelin' good about the two of us workin' together, suga', you got yourself drive to protect the people in this here city.<br><br>You get down there and <color orange>stop them Resistance from scamperin' off with those bombs.</color> I'll see if I can get some of my boys to bust into Altman's ball to arrest Pell for the little traitor that he is."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1636397060" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: You're the Monster </color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2353972223" "Stop the raid on Altman's warehouse"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1071242431" "You don't need to worry about things on my end, suga', you just need to make sure you're able to take care of things with the Resistance in Altman's warehouse."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3992565902" "Something doesn't seem right. There's no sign of the usual brute force the Resistance uses to break into buildings. The break in seems much too... refined."

